# Rust
**/target/

# .NET
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
# CI (hyper-pack-nuget.yml) arranges and packs these per-RID at pack time; regenerable
# locally via `cargo cdylib` (the csproj's runtimes/**/native/* wildcard item).
csharp/HyperCast/runtimes/
# The same for the static libraries a Native AOT publish links in: staged by the forge's
# static-libs/build-static-libs.sh at test and pack time, never committed.
csharp/HyperCast/staticlibs/
# go/staticlib's archives ARE committed — a Go module is whatever is in the tree — but only
# by stage-native-binaries.yml, which adds them with `git add -f` after verifying each one's
# build provenance. Ignored here so that a developer's own build of them (the forge's
# static-libs/build-static-libs.sh, which `go test` needs to link) can never
# ride into a commit by accident.
go/staticlib/*/*.a

# Gradle / Java
**/.gradle/
**/build/
# CI (hyper-publish-maven.yml) bundles all platforms' natives here at publish time; the
# local dev loop stages into build/generated-resources instead (already covered by
# **/build/ above), so anything here is regenerable via `cargo cdylib`.
java/src/main/resources/native/
# csharp/HyperCast/build/ is NuGet's real, tracked build/{PackageId}.targets packaging
# convention (auto-imported into every consumer for the browser-wasm NativeFileReference and
# EmccExportedFunction wiring — see HyperCast.csproj), not a build output. It collides with
# **/build/ above, which would otherwise silently swallow it: the file would sit on disk,
# pack correctly in a local `dotnet pack`, and simply never exist in CI. Each directory level
# needs its own negation — git won't descend into an excluded directory to find a deeper
# !file re-inclusion — and gitignore rules apply in file order, so this must come after the
# rule it un-ignores. HyperUuid carries the same block for the same reason.
!csharp/HyperCast/build/
!csharp/HyperCast/build/HyperCast.targets

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.venv/
**/dist/
**/.pytest_cache/
# The staged PyO3 extension for local dev/test — nested at hypercast._native (the maturin
# module-name), built from the core crate's python feature. abi3 wheels carry one build per
# platform regardless of Python version (hence the plain and .abi3 spellings, not a
# per-version-tagged glob); .pyd covers Windows.
python/src/hypercast/_native.so
python/src/hypercast/_native.abi3.so
python/src/hypercast/_native.pyd

# Swift
# The static libraries under swift/HyperCastCore.artifactbundle/{triple}/ are committed, not
# ignored — SwiftPM has no packing step for a git-URL dependency, unlike every other registry
# this repo publishes to — and only by stage-native-binaries.yml, after their provenance checks.
**/.build/

# Ruby
# CI places each leg's native lib here for `bundle exec rspec` at build-native time, and
# rubygems-publish stages all eight into the universal gem at gem-build time (the platform
# gems carry none); regenerable locally via `cargo cdylib`. Unlike the Go and Swift archives
# above, the gem build is a real packing step, so nothing here needs committing.
ruby/lib/hypercast/native/*/
ruby/Gemfile.lock
ruby/pkg/
ruby/.yardoc/
# The wasm32-wasip1 archives `rake wasm:gem` packs (and their .gz), staged from CI's
# ruby-wasm-<minor> artifacts by release.yml, or by hand; never committed.
ruby/ext/hypercast_native/*/
# rbwasm's interpreter build and its output, from running ruby/wasm-smoke locally.
ruby/wasm-smoke/Gemfile.lock
ruby/wasm-smoke/build/
ruby/wasm-smoke/rubies/
ruby/wasm-smoke/*.wasm
# Staged Magnus extension for local dev/test (built from the core crate's ruby feature;
# precompiled platform gems carry the real artifact).
ruby/lib/hypercast_native.so
ruby/lib/hypercast_native.bundle
# The per-ABI staging the fat platform gem is packed from (lib/hypercast/<minor>/), written
# by release.yml from CI artifacts. Same story as the flat pair above: build output, never
# committed. Scoped to the extension filename rather than the whole directory so it can't
# swallow a real lib/hypercast/*.rb source file if a minor-version-shaped one ever appears.
ruby/lib/hypercast/*/hypercast_native.so
ruby/lib/hypercast/*/hypercast_native.bundle

# PHP
# Native libs under php/src/native/{rid}/ are committed, not ignored — see
# php/src/native/README.md for why (Packagist has no packing step: the git tree at the tag
# IS the package).
php/vendor/
php/composer.lock
php/.phpunit.result.cache
# Root-level composer.json exists only for Packagist (see php/README.md's Install section) —
# nothing actually runs `composer install` from the repo root except a consumer's own build,
# but a stray local one shouldn't get committed either.
/vendor/
/composer.lock

# Node
**/node_modules/

# BenchmarkDotNet
# Writes output relative to the process's working directory when invoked via `dotnet run`
# rather than the project directory, so this can land almost anywhere in the tree — not just
# csharp/HyperCast.Benchmarks/. Criterion's own output already lands under rust/target/,
# covered by the **/target/ rule above.
**/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# IDE
.idea/
.vs/

# cargo-fuzz working state — the targets and Cargo.toml are tracked; the evolving corpus
# and any crash artifacts are machine-local (a reproducing crash gets minimized and
# committed as a regression test, not as a raw artifact).
rust/fuzz/corpus/
rust/fuzz/artifacts/
rust/fuzz/coverage/
